# pkg/ is a versioned deliverable, not a text directory.
#
# The artifact gate compares the committed bytes against a rebuild, byte for
# byte (verify-artifact.mjs gates [2] and [3]). This repository is authored from
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule git rewrites the
# wasm-bindgen JS/TS glue to CRLF on checkout while `build-wasm.sh` emits LF —
# and a clean Windows clone fails the freshness gate for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the source. `-text` disables eol translation entirely, so
# what is checked out is what was committed, on every platform.
#
# The .wasm is spared today only by git's NUL-byte heuristic. A deliverable that
# CI hashes should not depend on a heuristic, so it is marked explicitly.
pkg/** -text
pkg/*.wasm binary

# Run by `bash` in CI and by hand on Windows. A CRLF checkout makes bash fail on
# the shebang line with a message that names neither the file nor the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
